  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14120255/assets/c22d8afca77121e994303cc67c6e85b065b452a5725603dec04273d1c8d427b3.png)\n\nExpress the relation $R⊆A\\times A$ represented by the mapping diagram above as a set of ordered pairs.\n\n$R={(a,b),(b,$\n{{field-1}}$),(c,a),($\n{{field-2}}$,d),($\n{{field-3}}$,b)}$",
  "worked_solution": "The ordered pairs belonging to our relation correspond to the arrows on the mapping diagram. Each arrow starts at the first component of the pair and ends at its second component.\n\nOur diagram has the following arrows:\n\n- Arrows starting from $a:$\n\n- $a\\to b,$ so the relation contains the pair $(a,b).$\n\n- Arrows starting from $b:$\n\n- $b\\to b,$ so the relation contains the pair $(b,b).$\n\n- Arrows starting from $c:$\n\n- $c\\to a$ and $c\\to d,$ so the relation contains the pairs $(c,a)$ and $(c,d).$\n\n- Arrows starting from $d:$\n\n- $d\\to b,$ so the relation contains the pair $(d,b).$\n\nTherefore, $R$ contains the following ordered pairs:\n\n$$\nR={(a,b),(b,b),(c,a),(c,d),(d,b)}\n$$",
